issue.body:
Using vgpu 0.2.0 on Node 22.18.0 and Ubuntu 24.04, a 16x16 solid red shader renders RGB values correctly but every output alpha value is 0. The same script produced opaque pixels in 0.1.9. Expected alpha 255; actual alpha 0. I can reproduce on two clean machines and included the minimal shader and JavaScript inline below.

JavaScript: import { render } from 'vgpu'; await render({ width: 16, height: 16, shader: source, output: 'out.png' });
Shader fragment result: vec4f(1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0).
